{"course": {"schema_version": "1.0", "course_id": "mitocw-15-649-spring-2003", "institution": "Massachusetts Institute of Technology", "platform": "MIT OpenCourseWare", "course_codes": ["15.649"], "cross_listed_codes": [], "course_title": "The Law of Mergers and Acquisitions", "course_slug": "15-649-the-law-of-mergers-and-acquisitions-spring-2003", "term": "Spring", "year": 2003, "as_taught_in": "Spring 2003", "language": "en", "departments": ["Sloan School of Management"], "academic_levels": ["Graduate"], "instructors": ["Dr. John Akula"], "subject_primary": "Finance", "subject_secondary": ["Industrial Relations and Human Resource Management", "Social Science", "Legal Studies"], "topic_tree": [{"name": "Business", "subtopics": [{"name": "Finance", "specialties": []}, {"name": "Industrial Relations and Human Resource Management", "specialties": []}]}, {"name": "Social Science", "subtopics": [{"name": "Legal Studies", "specialties": []}]}], "topic_keywords": [], "pedagogy_tags": [], "assessment_types": [], "course_feature_tags": ["Lecture Notes", "Written Assignments"], "description": "This course is designed to give students an introduction to the law-sensitive aspects of Mergers & Acquisitions (M&A). In Module I, we examine the legal implications of key roles and deal structures, and walk through some of the issues that would typically arise in a simple and friendly transaction. We also give a class to the legal issues arising in LBOs and the legal concerns of financial sponsors more generally, and another class to employment-related issues, including those relating to managers facing unsettled circumstances. In Module II, we look at a variety of complications, including those that arise in the friendly or unfriendly purchase of a publicly-held company; deals involving distressed and hi-tech companies; antitrust concerns; allegations of misconduct by management or board members; and deals involving non-U.S. companies.", "course_url": "https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/15